quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  17,76,"And they had (also) sought to unsettle you in the land (of Mecca) to expel you from it, (but Allah Himself caused you to migrate by His Divine Plan). But in that case, they would not have remained after you (had left) except a little."
  17,77,"Such was (Our) custom regarding those We had sent from among Our messengers before you, and you will not find any change in Our custom."
  17,78,"Establish the (ritual) prayer from the declining of the sun till the darkening of the night, and (observe particularly) the dawn recitation. Indeed, the dawn recitation is witnessed (by angels)."
  17,79,"And during a part of the night, offer an additional prayer as an act of extra devotion for you. Surely, your Lord will raise you to a praiseworthy station."
  17,80,"And say: ‘My Lord! Make me enter with an honourable entrance, and make me depart with an honourable departure, and grant me a favourable authority from Your Presence.’"
  17,81,"And say: ‘The truth has come, and falsehood has vanished. Indeed, falsehood is bound to vanish.’"
  17,82,And We send down in the Qur’an that which is a healing and a mercy for the believers. And it increases the wrongdoers in nothing but loss.
  17,83,"And whenever We bestow favour upon human being, he becomes disregardful and turns aside arrogantly. But whenever harm befalls him, he loses hope."
  17,84,Say: ‘Each acts according to his character.’ Your Lord knows best who is better guided on the way.
  17,85,"And they ask you about the spirit. Say: ‘The spirit is from (the realm of) the Command of my Lord, and you have not been given knowledge but a little.’"
  17,86,"If We wished, We could have certainly taken away what We have revealed to you. Then you would not find for yourself any guardian against Us."
